[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67975,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This generic category includes a select group of sarcoma entities composed of undifferentiated small round cells, including Ewing sarcoma, <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcoma, sarcoma with <em>BCOR</em> genetic alterations, and round cell sarcoma with <em>EWSR1</em>&ndash;non-ETS fusions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67976,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9364/3 Ewing sarcoma</p>\r\n<p>9367/3 <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcoma</p>\r\n<p>9368/3 Sarcoma with <em>BCOR</em> genetic alterations</p>\r\n<p>9366/3 Round cell sarcoma with <em>EWSR1</em>&ndash;non-ETS fusions</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67977,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "<p>2C29.1 &amp; XH85G7 Other specified malignant neoplasms of other or ill-defined sites in the respiratory system or intrathoracic organs &amp; Round cell sarcoma, undifferentiated</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:44:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67978,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Askin tumour; Ewing-like sarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67979,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67980,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ewing sarcoma and <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>PATZ1</em> sarcoma not infrequently involve the chest wall {31189996}, whereas the thoracic cavity is an uncommon primary site {26685084; 28877060; 29431183; 31189996; 31647130}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67981,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chest wall tumours may be detected as masses, whereas patients with intrathoracic tumours present with cough, dyspnoea, pain, or other symptoms related to tumour location {22802134}. Some tumours are detected incidentally {26698372}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67982,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours typically occur in children or young adults, but patients of any age can be affected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67983,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67984,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "<p>Ewing sarcoma characteristically exhibits a fusion of <em>EWSR1</em> or <em>FUS</em> to an ETS gene family member (e.g. <em>FLI1</em> or <em>ERG</em>). <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcomas harbour <em>CIC</em> rearrangement, most commonly <em>CIC</em>-<em>DUX4</em> {24723486}. Sarcoma with <em>BCOR</em> genetic alterations features either <em>BCOR</em> fusions (to <em>CCNB3</em> or other partners) or internal tandem duplication (ITD) of <em>BCOR</em> exon&nbsp;15 {26752546; 26945340; 31647130}. <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>NFATC2</em> (less commonly <em>FUS</em>-<em>NFATC2</em>) and <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>PATZ1</em> are the fusion genes seen in round cell sarcomas with <em>EWSR1</em>&ndash;non-ETS fusions.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:45:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67985,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Most undifferentiated round cell sarcomas are large, grey-tan soft masses with necrosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:45:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67986,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ewing sarcoma consists of uniform small round cells, which are often positive for CD99 and NKX2-2 {22446943}. <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcoma shows lobulated growth of minimally pleomorphic round to epithelioid cells, commonly immunopositive for ETV4 and WT1 {24723486; 26685084; 27443513}. Sarcomas with <em>BCOR</em> genetic alterations are composed of uniform oval to spindle cells within variably vascular fibro-oedematous stroma, positive for BCOR {27428733}. <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>PATZ1</em> sarcoma features round to spindle cells within a fibrous background and with variable expression of myogenic and neurogenic markers {31189996; 30379650}. Cords/nests/trabeculae of round cells in a fibromyxoid stroma characterize <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>NFATC2</em> sarcomas {30994538; 31078563}.</p>\r\n<p>For additional details, see the <em>Soft tissue and bone tumours</em> volume of this series [[WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Soft tissue and bone tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2020. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 3). https://publications.iarc.fr/588.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67987,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67988,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The specific genetic abnormalities are detectable by a variety of molecular methods.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67989,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Undifferentiated small round cell morphology</li>\r\n<li>Genetic confirmation for round cell sarcoma with <em>EWSR1</em>&ndash;non-ETS fusions</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Genetic confirmation for Ewing sarcoma, <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcoma, and sarcomas with <em>BCOR</em> genetic alterations</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:45:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67990,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) or American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system may be used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67991,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 215,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Undifferentiated small round cell sarcomas are generally associated with poor outcome. For Ewing sarcoma, stage, anatomical location, and pathological response to neoadjuvant chemotherapy are prognostic factors {27482030}. <em>CIC</em>-rearranged sarcomas have more aggressive behaviour than Ewing sarcoma {26685084; 28346326}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]